apital himself but this is not  true  i mean just think about it he spent the  vast majority of his adult life in  academia  now i'm sure that rj put in every penny  he had but most of the money for initial  development actually came from the  florida government you see rj's father  roberts karen senior was a business  owner himself who ran a company called  mainstream engineering i think you can  see where rj got the name mainstream  motors from but anyway his father had  managed to raise 61 million over 25  years all from the us government so his  father was well aware of how to raise  money and given that the u.s government  was looking to support evie endeavors rj  was able to secure a small grant of 2  million  given that he was building a car from  scratch though this really didn't last  that long  rj ended up spending 900 thousand  dollars on payroll 170 000 on  contractors and the rest was presumably  spent on materials and manufacturing by  2011 rj had burned through all the money  but at least he had something to show  for it mainstream motors had created an  electric sports car called the r1 but  there was a massive problem which was  the tesla roadster rj's sports car  wasn't bad by any means but the roadster  was already on the road and it didn't  make sense to compete against tesla in  an already niche market  i'm not sure why rj didn't realize this  when he started the project as tesla was  delivering roadster since 2008 but he  did eventually make this realization and  he would decide to scrap the entire idea  now i'm sure people are going to comment  down below that ravine is considering  bringing back this car today so it  wasn't a waste but in 2011 the revival  of this car was by no means a guarantee  so rj was back to ground zero  [Music]  determined to change the direction of  the company rj looked at what ev  competitors weren't targeting and the  obvious answer was suvs and pickup  trucks rj also decided to change the  name of the company to rivien which was  derived from indian river he combined  the first part of river and the last  part of indian rj had spent a lot of his  childhood in a row boat on the indian  river in florida hence the name  anyway rj had a new target and a new  name but he was still lacking the  biggest part which was new funding for  rj though this wasn't that hard to  secure the source of rivie's 2012  funding effort isn't clear but it was  likely the government again or some  venture capitalists would like to keep a  low profile  over the next couple of years rivian  hired a bunch of talent from legacy  automakers like ford gm and chrysler and  by the end of 2016 they had grown to 100  employees  this is still relatively small but given  that basically all of these guys were  engineers earning six figures it wasn't  cheap to run rivian  even if we just assume a hundred  thousand dollars per year per person  we're looking at 10 million annually on  just payroll and keep in mind riven  still had no revenue coming in in the  meantime ravion was also investing  heavily into manufacturing plants for  example in january of 2017 rivian  acquired a manufacturing plant from  mitsubishi for 16 million dollars soon  enough raven revealed their pickup truck  android suv originally called the a1t  and the a1c at the la auto show in  november of 2018.  unlike the cyber truck reveal which left  the audience divided the a1t and a1c  were exactly what the audience wanted  from a distance they looked just like  traditional vehicles but up close they  had that futuristic electric style and  that's what made all the difference  rivien was slowly getting ready to  launch their first vehicle but the last  step of bringing the product to market  would take way longer and cost way more  than anybody expected fortunately for  rivien though investors with massive  pockets would enter the scene after this  reveal  up until this point riven had primarily  raised money in the tens of millions but  it didn't take long for them to cross  into the hundreds of millions in may of  2018 rivian took on 200 million worth of  debt from standard chartered bank which  increased the total raised funds to a  whopping 450 million dollars despite  raising nearly half a billion dollars  the general public still wasn't that  interested in evs as the price was still  way out of reach for most people but all  of this would change with the launch of  the tesla model 3 in 2017. while the  tesla model 3 was a promising idea from  the start many big players weren't  convinced that tesla would actually be  able to execute on the idea  and this was an absolutely fair  assessment given that tesla would go to  production held in 2018. tesla played  with the bankruptcy line several times  this year and there were plenty of  customer complaints regarding subpar  manufacturing despite all the  uncertainty though tesla survived 2018  and that was the signal that the time  for evs had to finally come  many big players didn't want to take the  gamble with tesla but now that tesla had  gone to the other side they were willing  to take the risk with other eb startups  and this led them straight to rivien in  february of 2019 amazon led a 700  million dollar investment round for  rivien overnight riven went from  lifetime fundraising of 450 million  dollars to raising 700 million dollars  in a single round and this was just the  beginning just two months later ford  invested 500 million dollars which they  would later raise to 1.2 billion dollars  later that year cox automotive poured in  another 350 million dollars and amazon  would put the nail on the coffin by  ordering 100 000 electric delivery  vehicles from rivien by the end of 2019  ravine had raised a total of 2.85  billion dollars and now that smart money  was in it was time to open up the gates  as we all know starting at the end of  2019 tesla stock soared first it crossed  a hundred billion dollars then overtook  volkswagen and toyota and now it's  literally a trillion dollar company  that's more than the rest of the top 10  auto companies combined i'm not trying  to get into whether that's justified or  not but something that's crystal clear  is the fact that tesla took the rest of  the ev industry with them and that of  course includes rivien  in the meantime it ravine was trying to  start production and get deliveries  going promised delivery dates came and  went and rivian kept delaying the  release time after time but one thing we  can be sure of was that money was no  longer the issue they had already raised  billions and the billions were flowing  in due to tesla hype but rivien was  running out of time  ford had reviewed their f-150 lightning  and tesla was rapidly building their  austin gigafactory and making the cyber  truck a reality  it would have been a shame that riven  had targeted the eevee pickup truck and  suv market a decade ago just to be beat  by tesla and ford luckily for rivien  though they were able to deliver in the  last second at the end of august riven  filed for 80 billion ipo and this  confirmed that rifian was finally ready  to start making deliveries  ironically despite targeting the market  years before ford and tesla it looks  like they only beat them to market by  months  anyway by the time riven ipo'd they had  raised a total of 10.5 billion dollars  since 2019 alone to put that in  perspective it that's half the valuation  of nissan twice the valuation of a mazda  and four times evaluation of ashton  martin and all of that was just to get  their first product to market but  looking back that was just a drop in the  bucket given that they would reach a  valuation of 150 billion dollars which  just leaves one question what's next  the truth is that riven's entire  existence has been a bubble first it was  millions from the government then it was  tens of millions from early investors  then it was hundreds of millions from  smart money and now it's billions from  the public markets it seems like this  must come to an end soon but the truth  is that's not necessarily the case all  it takes is one announcement from elon  that tesla is going to do stocks play on  december 9th and tesla and the ev  industry will go to mars if tesla makes  another one i wouldn't be surprised if  raven ends up overtaking toyota which is  stupid but reality nonetheless  when the bubble does eventually pop  though whether that's tomorrow or after  reaping reaches a trillion dollar  evaluation most regional investors will  likely lose substantial amounts of money  instead of crashing on rivien and  shoring the stock though i think it's a  much better idea to see it in a positive  light the eevee bubble has given  companies that would otherwise have  little chance against the legacy  automakers and opportunity and at the  end of the day the bubble is centered on  a great cause which is reducing  pollution and transitioning to  sustainable energy the more companies  that enter the scene and fight for  market share the faster we'll see a  transition to evs so maybe the bubble  isn't actually all that bad the crash  however will be deadly peruvian if they  don't make a mark before it's too late  so i wish riven the best despite their  stupid valuation but only time will tell  if they're able to make it to the other  side  do you guys think rivien will survive  the eventual crash and rival tesla  comment that down below  also drop a like if you have a love-hate  relationship with the eevee bubble and  of course consider joining our discord  community to suggest future video ideas  and consider subscribing to see more  questions logically answered but until  then i'm hari and i'll see you guys on  the next one

